+/**
+ * SLICC patch (ai-ecoverse/slicc#2710, #2735): packfile integrity verification,
+ * extracted so it can be memoized as a promise on the cached pack index.
+ *
+ * Upstream ran this inline behind a `p._checksumVerified` boolean that is only
+ * set AFTER the `await`, so every reader that arrived while the first
+ * verification was in flight started its own SHA-1 over the whole pack (a
+ * 92 MB pack was hashed 8-9 times per command). Callers now await a single
+ * shared promise.
+ *
+ * The deep (full-payload) SHA-1 is skipped when the caller's cache object sets
+ * `skipDeepPackVerification` — the O(1) trailer check still runs, matching what
+ * canonical git does on a normal object read (it only verifies packs on
+ * `fsck` / `index-pack`).
